// title: VossstartDay1
// ---
// <<jump playtestNode>>
// This is an example/Reference of how to set up dialog

// The first node of Dialog MUST be named in this manner
// The Starting Node set in the NPCData scriptable object attached
// to the npcInteract
// AND 'startDay1' or 'startDay2/3/4' depending on what day this dialog is for

// ! its best to keep all dialog for a character across days on one big YS script,
// and break it up into different days instead of multiple scripts

// How to check if player has an item?

// You can check if the player has obtained evidence that has either been
// SCANNED or NOT SCANNED using this command. 

// <<if HasItem("objectID")>>
// if the player has that object then anything written here
// will be run 

// ! the objectID is the OBJECT HOLDERS NAME 
// ^ the inspectable object that has the interactableObj script 
// NOT ITS CHILD 
// <<endif>>

// ! if you want to check if the player has an item that 
// WAS SCANNED. then you run this command a little differently.
// <<if HasItem("objectID_scan")>>

// ! this will be the same objectID but with _scan 
// ^^^ do not edit the gameobject's name to include _scan,
// the scripts will automatically add it to inventory with that 

// <<endif>>

// <<jump VOSSintro>>
// ===

// title: VOSSintro
// ---
// <<AddNPC "VOSS">>
// REEVES: Voss Axiom, 42. She’s the COO of Axiom Networks.
// LENNOX: Nova Axiom’s eldest daughter, then?
// REEVES: She is. She supposedly helped organize the party; encouraged it even, with the help of her husband.
// LENNOX: Why would she even be on this list? Shouldn’t she have already been interviewed?
// REEVES: Should’ve been, yes. She refused to participate in any kind of interviews while in mourning. We had to press hard just for her to agree to come here today.
// LENNOX: Sounds like a delightful character.
// -> *Approach.*
//     VOSS: Hm? Can I help you?
//     LENNOX: Considering this an investigation, I assume we can help each other, actually.
//     VOSS: Oh? Are you the new investigator? 
//     LENNOX: For the remainder of this case, yes.
//     VOSS: How delightful. I hope you aren't as incompetent as the others.
// -> *Move on.*
//     LENNOX: Let's move on.
//     //<<jump ActOneSceneTwoDashTwo>>
// ===

// title: VossSpeakstartDay1
// ---
// VOSS: I see you're done with your snooping around, Lysander.
// VOSS: In which case I suppose I'm next on the chopping block?
// -> *Ask about her*
//     VOSS: What business do you have to know about me? You’re here to find out what happened to my idiot brother.
//     //LENNOX:
//     -> *Persist.*
//         VOSS: Lovely, you’re one of those.
//         VOSS: What would you even want to know that isn't already globally known?
//         VOSS: Eldest Daughter of Nova Axiom, PR rep, planning, syncing. 
//         VOSS: There’s nothing special to it. I’m just a woman who keeps up with her job.
//     -> *Let up.*
//         VOSS: That's what I figured.
// -> *Ask about the party.*
//         LENNOX: Where were you located during the after party?
//         VOSS: Wouldn't that be in one of your little files?
//         LENNOX: I want to hear from you directly where you were during the party.
//         VOSS: I was speaking to my mother and Cipher in the dining room. 
//         VOSS: We were discussing logistics about Cipher taking the new position.
//         LENNOX: I see.
//         -> What of when he passed on, then?
//             VOSS: ...I was franyly taken aback.
//             VOSS: I watched him take a sip of his drink then choke.
//             VOSS: He dropped his glass, scratched at his neck, then fell to the ground.
//             VOSS: It was...
//             VOSS: ..I-I don't have words.
//             -> And afterwards?
//                 VOSS: I didn't stay for "an afterwards".
//                 VOSS: I just, left.
// -> *Ask about the victim.*
//     LENNOX: Tell me abourt Cipher.
//     VOSS: Don't you have a file for that?
//     LENNOX: I believe personal relationships matter here as well.
//     VOSS: ...as a person, he's stupid. Reckless, and impulsive.
//     VOSS: But he has a heart of gold. Which is rare to see in this city.
//     VOSS: Always wanting to help those who couldn't help themselves.
//     VOSS: Had mom not wanted to retire, I'm sure he would've kept on with what he was doing.
//     -> Who was Cipher to you?
//         VOSS: …How do you mean?
//         LENNOX: Beyond being your brother; What did he mean to you?
//         VOSS: Sometimes, it's done him a lot of good, others, not so much. 
//         VOSS: The last stupid thing he did…he was trying to make up for it. 
//         -> Stupid thing?
//             VOSS: Monumentally. 
//             VOSS: He never told me the specifics, but I trusted him. 
//             VOSS: I know he just wanted to help someone who didn't have the means.
//             VOSS: It feels as if him having a big heart got him targeted and killed.
//             VOSS: As stupid as he was…Cipher didn’t deserve that. At all.



// ===
title: VossQuestions
---
// <<if HasItem("Wrist Watch")>>
// -> *Show her the wrist watch.*
//     VOSS: Oh. That old thing? It was a gift Cipher gave to the sleazeball a few years back.
//     -> Drift?
//         VOSS: Precisely
//         -> A gift? For what?
//             VOSS: From what Cipher said, Draco pulled off something huge for him. That watch was a thank you. 
//             VOSS: Besides, let's be realistic. Drift couldn’t afford something like this.
//             -> You're implying the existence of an interesting bond.
//                 VOSS: Who am I to say? Cipher always had an interesting fixation for strays. Much to the family’s dismay. 
//                 VOSS: It’s never ended well, and now look at him.
===
// <<endif>>

